--- stdout

[1mduplicate-function[0m  [2mshared/duplication[0m
  Two functions repeat the same body

[33mWhy it is a sin[0m

  Code that represents one decision, mechanism or folder should say what it means in one
  place.

[33mHow to fix it[0m

  Write a shared function and call it from the places that need it.
  Move the copied body to one owner and delegate to it from each caller.

[33mExample[0m

  In PHP:
  
  ```php
  ----------[ Bad ]----------
  
  // in Shop\Catalog\StockDigest
  public function fingerprint(int $base, int $count): string
  {
      $total = $base;
  
      for ($i = 0; $i < $count; $i++) {
          $total += $i * 2;
      }
  
      return md5((string) $total);
  }
  
  // in Shop\Customers\LoyaltyDigest
  public function fingerprint(int $base, int $count): string
  {
      $total = $base;
  
      for ($i = 0; $i < $count; $i++) {
          $total += $i * 2;
      }
  
      return md5((string) $total);
  }
  
  // in Shop\Orders\CancellationNote
  public function __construct(?string $code)
  {
      $this->code = $code ?? Str::uuid()->toString();
  }
  
  // in Shop\Orders\DispatchNote
  public function __construct(?string $code)
  {
      $this->code = $code ?? Str::uuid()->toString();
  }
  
  // in Shop\Reporting\SalesDigest
  public function fingerprint(int $base, int $count): string
  {
      $total = $base;
  
      for ($i = 0; $i < $count; $i++) {
          $total += $i * 2;
      }
  
      return md5((string) $total);
  }
  
  ----------[ Good ]----------
  
  public static function of(int $base, int $count): string
  {
      $steps = array_map(static fn (int $i): int => $i * 2, range(0, max(0, $count - 1)));
  
      return md5((string) ($base + array_sum($steps)));
  }
  ```
  
